# Multiply Strings

**LeetCode Problem:** [Multiply Strings](https://leetcode.com/problems/multiply-strings/)

## Approach: Array Simulation (Grade School Multiplication)

1. First, handle the edge case where either number is `"0"`. Return `"0"` directly.
2. Create a result array of size `n1 + n2` initialized with zeros because the maximum length of the product can be `n1 + n2`.
3. Traverse both strings from right to left and multiply each pair of digits.
4. Add the multiplication result to the corresponding position in the result array.
5. Store the current digit using `sum % 10` and carry using `sum / 10`.
6. Skip leading zeros from the result array and convert the remaining digits into a string.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    string multiply(string num1, string num2) {
        int n1 = num1.length(), n2 = num2.length();

        if(num1 == "0" || num2 == "0") return "0";

        vector<int> digit(n1 + n2, 0);

        for(int i = n1 - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            for(int j = n2 - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
                int mul = (num1[i] - '0') * (num2[j] - '0');
                int sum = mul + digit[i + j + 1];

                digit[i + j + 1] = sum % 10;
                digit[i + j] += sum / 10;
            }
        }

        int index = 0;
        string ans = "";

        while(index < digit.size() && digit[index] == 0)
            index++;

        while(index < digit.size()) {
            ans += (digit[index] + '0');
            index++;
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(n1 \times n2)\) — We multiply every digit of `num1` with every digit of `num2`.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(n1 + n2)\) — We use an extra array to store the resulting digits.

